### Suggested Fix:

To fix these issues, you can add null checks for the `start` and `end` parameters in the `checkStartsWith` and `checkEndsWith` methods, respectively. Here is an example of how you can modify the methods:

```java
public boolean checkStartsWith(String str, String start) {
    if (str == null || start == null) {
        return false;
    }
    return str.regionMatches(!sensitive, 0, start, 0, start.length());
}

public boolean checkEndsWith(String str, String end) {
    if (str == null || end == null) {
        return false;
    }
    final int endLen = end.length();
    return str.regionMatches(!sensitive, str.length() - endLen, end, 0, endLen);
}
```

By adding these null checks, you can prevent the NullPointerExceptions and ensure that the methods handle null values correctly.
